{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.collatz_one_odd_family","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.collatz_one_odd_family","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":31,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.genNoCycle_of_lead","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.genNoCycle_of_lead","kind":"theorem","line":639,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L639-L666","doc":"**Uniform spread exclusion.** A cyclic word of `m + 1` odd steps whose last\neven run `r m` is large enough — `3^{m+1} ≤ 2^{r m + m}` — has **no cycle**,\nfor ANY arrangement of the other runs. Subsumes every per-rung `of_lead`\ncorollary at once (the spread half of the `q`-Steiner endgame). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.genSteinerNumZ_le_lead","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.genSteinerNumZ_le_lead","kind":"theorem","line":627,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L627-L637","doc":"**Tight bound** `M_{m+1} ≤ 2^{runSum m}·(3^{m+1} − 2^{m+1})` — the numerator is\nbounded independently of the last run `r m` (only `runSum r m` enters). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.genSteinerNumZ_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.genSteinerNumZ_le","kind":"theorem","line":601,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L601-L625","doc":"**Loose bound** `M_m ≤ 2^{runSum m}·(3^m − 2^m)` (clean induction). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.genSteinerNumZ_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.genSteinerNumZ_pos","kind":"theorem","line":594,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L594-L599","doc":"`0 < M_{m+1}` — the numerator of a nonempty cyclic word is positive\n(discharges the `hpos` hypothesis of `genNoCycle`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.genSteinerNumZ_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.genSteinerNumZ_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":586,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L586-L592","doc":"`0 ≤ M_m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.genNoCycle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.genNoCycle","kind":"theorem","line":554,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L554-L573","doc":"**Uniform `q`-Steiner exclusion.** For any cyclic word of `m` odd steps whose\n`q = 1` numerator height `M_m = genSteinerNumZ r m` is positive and strictly\nbelow the denominator height `2^{runSum m + m} − 3^m`, there is no cycle: the\ndenominator cannot divide the smaller positive numerator. This is the uniform\nengine — every rung's `no_*_cycle` is an instance (compute `M_m` and check the\ngap). The remaining `q`-Steiner content is purely arithmetic: which\narrangements satisfy the gap. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.genSteinerNum_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.genSteinerNum_map","kind":"theorem","line":544,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L544-L552","doc":"**The `q = 1` evaluation sends `N_m` to `M_m`.** For any ring hom\n`φ : R →+* ℤ` with `φ q = 1`, `φ (genSteinerNum q r m) = genSteinerNumZ r m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.genSteinerNumZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.genSteinerNumZ","kind":"def","line":537,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L537-L542","doc":"The `q = 1` image of the `q`-Steiner numerator: `M₀ = 0`,\n`M_{m+1} = 3·M_m + 2^{runSum m + m}`. This is `φ(N_m)` for any `q = 1`\nevaluation `φ` (see `genSteinerNum_map`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.genForced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.genForced","kind":"theorem","line":526,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L526-L535","doc":"**Uniform `q`-Steiner forced equation.** A cyclic word (`v m = v 0`) of `m`\nodd steps with even runs `r` pins its value:\n`((q+1)^{runSum m + m} − [3]^m)·v 0 = N_m`. Specialises to every rung above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.genOddChain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.genOddChain","kind":"theorem","line":505,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L505-L524","doc":"**General odd-chain collapse (arbitrary even runs).** Given the per-step\nrelations `(q+1)^{r i + 1}·v(i+1) = [3]·v i + 1`, the chain of `m` odd steps\ntelescopes to `(q+1)^{runSum m + m}·v m = [3]^m·v 0 + N_m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.genSteinerNum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.genSteinerNum","kind":"def","line":499,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L499-L503","doc":"The `q`-Steiner numerator for a cyclic word of `m` odd steps with runs `r`:\n`N₀ = 0`, `N_{m+1} = [3]·N_m + (q+1)^{runSum m + m}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.runSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.runSum","kind":"def","line":494,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L494-L497","doc":"Partial sum of the first `m` even runs, `runSum r m = r 0 + ⋯ + r (m-1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_no_four_odd_cycle_of_lead","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_no_four_odd_cycle_of_lead","kind":"theorem","line":454,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L454-L480","doc":"**No four-odd-step cycle with leading even run `a ≥ 4`.** Unconditional: when\nthe leading run is `a ≥ 4` the denominator height `2^{a+b+c+d+4} − 81`\ndominates (`2^{a+1} ≥ 32` times the top numerator term), so the height gap of\n`qcollatz_no_four_odd_cycle` holds for every `b, c, d`. By rotation-invariance\nthis excludes every four-odd word possessing an even run of length `≥ 4` — the\ngeneric spread regime for `k_odd = 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_no_four_odd_cycle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_no_four_odd_cycle","kind":"theorem","line":433,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L433-L452","doc":"**No four-odd-step cycle when the height obstruction fires.** Given the\nexplicit `q = 1` height gap\n`27 + 9·2^{b+1} + 3·2^{b+c+2} + 2^{b+c+d+3} < 2^{a+b+c+d+4} − 81`, the forced\nequation has no solution: the denominator `2^{a+b+c+d+4} − 81` cannot divide\nthe strictly-smaller positive numerator. Fires for the spread arrangements. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_four_odd_forces","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_four_odd_forces","kind":"theorem","line":384,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L384-L431","doc":"**Four separated odd steps force their denominator equation.**\n`E^a O E^b O E^c O E^d O` (four odd steps, even runs `a, b, c, d`) forces\n`((q+1)^{a+b+c+d+4} − (q²+q+1)⁴)·x\n    = (q²+q+1)³ + (q²+q+1)²·(q+1)^{b+1} + (q²+q+1)·(q+1)^{b+c+2}\n      + (q+1)^{b+c+d+3}`. The `mᵢ` are the intermediate cycle values;\n`heven*`/`hodd*` are the even-collapse and odd-step relations, chained\ncyclically. Same telescoping as `qcollatz_three_odd_forces`, one level\ndeeper. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_no_three_odd_cycle_of_lead","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_no_three_odd_cycle_of_lead","kind":"theorem","line":347,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L347-L372","doc":"**No three-odd-step cycle with leading even run `a ≥ 3`.** A clean\nunconditional exclusion: when the leading run is `a ≥ 3` the denominator\nheight `2^{a+b+c+3} − 27` dominates the numerator height (`2^{a+1} ≥ 16` times\nthe top term), so the height gap of `qcollatz_no_three_odd_cycle` holds for\nevery `b, c`. By rotation-invariance of cycles this excludes every three-odd\nword possessing an even run of length `≥ 3` — the generic spread regime. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_no_three_odd_cycle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_no_three_odd_cycle","kind":"theorem","line":325,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L325-L345","doc":"**No three-odd-step cycle when the height obstruction fires.** Given the\nexplicit `q = 1` height gap `9 + 3·2^{b+1} + 2^{b+c+2} < 2^{a+b+c+3} − 27`\n(numerator height strictly below denominator height), the forced equation has\nno solution: `2^{a+b+c+3} − 27` cannot divide the smaller positive numerator.\nThis is the honest general application — it fires for the *spread*\narrangements; the clustered ones are rotations of tails (see\n`qcollatz_no_adj_tail_cycle`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_three_odd_forces","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_three_odd_forces","kind":"theorem","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L288-L323","doc":"**Three separated odd steps force their denominator equation.**\n`E^a O E^b O E^c O` (even runs `a, b, c`, three odd steps) forces\n`((q+1)^{a+b+c+3} − (q²+q+1)³)·x\n    = (q²+q+1)² + (q²+q+1)·(q+1)^{b+1} + (q+1)^{b+c+2}`. The variables\n`m2, m4` are the two intermediate cycle values entering the second and third\nodd steps; `heven*`/`hodd*` are the even-collapse and odd-step relations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_no_two_odd_cycle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_no_two_odd_cycle","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L238-L258","doc":"**No two-odd-step cycle of period `k ≥ 5`.** The `q=1` height of the\ndenominator `2^{a+b+2} − 9` exceeds the numerator height `3 + 2^{b+1}` for\nevery arrangement `b` once `a+b+2 ≥ 5`, so the divisibility fails. This\nexcludes **all** two-odd-step words (adjacent or separated) of period `≥ 5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_two_odd_forces","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_two_odd_forces","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L214-L236","doc":"**Two separated odd steps force their denominator equation.** `E^a O E^b O`\nforces `((q+1)^{a+b+2} − (q²+q+1)²)·x = (q²+q+1) + (q+1)^{b+1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_no_adj_tail_cycle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_no_adj_tail_cycle","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L183-L203","doc":"**No adjacent-tail cycle when `2^k > 2·3^m`.** The `q=1` height of the\ndenominator is `2^k − 3^m`, against numerator height `3^m − 2^m`; the\ncontractive bound `2·3^m < 2^k` forces `2^k − 3^m > 3^m − 2^m > 0`, so the\ndivisibility fails. Excludes the entire `E^{k-m}O^m` family in that range —\nthe general infinite result subsuming the one- and two-odd-step cases. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_adj_tail_forces","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_adj_tail_forces","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L168-L181","doc":"**General adjacent-tail forcing.** For an `m`-step odd chain `Q` closing via an\neven tail of length `k−m` (`Q_m = (q+1)^{k-m}·Q₀`), the cycle forces\n`((q+1)^k − (q²+q+1)^m)·Q₀ = Sₘ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.oddTailSum_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.oddTailSum_map","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L158-L166","doc":"**`q=1` height of `Sₘ` is `3^m − 2^m`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.odd_chain_collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.odd_chain_collapse","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L142-L156","doc":"**Odd chain closed form.** An `m`-step odd chain `Qⱼ₊₁(q+1) = [3]Qⱼ + 1`\nsatisfies `(q+1)^m · Q_m = [3]^m · Q₀ + Sₘ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.oddTailSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.oddTailSum","kind":"def","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L137-L140","doc":"`Sₘ = Σ_{j<m} [3]^j (q+1)^{m-1-j}`, via `Sₘ₊₁ = [3]·Sₘ + (q+1)^m`, `S₀ = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_no_two_odd_adj_cycle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_no_two_odd_adj_cycle","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L109-L126","doc":"**No two-adjacent-odd-step cycle of period `k ≥ 4`.** The `q = 1` height of the\ndenominator `(q+1)^k − (q²+q+1)²` is `2^k − 9`, against numerator height `5`;\nbut `2^k − 9 ∤ 5` for `k ≥ 4` (`|2^k − 9| ≥ 7 > 5`). A second infinite family,\nby the same height engine. (`k = 3` is `EOO`, handled by the period-3\nword-elimination, where `2³ − 9 = −1` is a unit.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_two_odd_adj_forces","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_two_odd_adj_forces","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L93-L107","doc":"**Two adjacent odd steps force their denominator equation.** The word\n`E^{k-2}OO` forces `((q+1)^k − (q²+q+1)²)·P_{k-2} = q²+2q+2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.no_cycle_of_q_one_height","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.no_cycle_of_q_one_height","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L87-L91","doc":"**Generic `q = 1` height obstruction.** If a cycle forces `D·P = n` and some\n`q = 1` evaluation `φ : R →+* ℤ` has `φ(D) ∤ φ(n)`, there is no such cycle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_no_one_odd_cycle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_no_one_odd_cycle","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L63-L80","doc":"**No one-odd-step cycle of period `k ≥ 3`.** Given any `q = 1` evaluation\n`φ : R →+* ℤ`, the forced denominator equation `((q+1)^k−(q²+q+1))·P = 1`\nmaps to `(2^k − 3)·φ(P) = 1`, making `2^k − 3` a unit of `ℤ`; but\n`2^k − 3 ∉ {±1}` for `k ≥ 3`. So the family `E^{k-1}O` has no nontrivial\ncycle at any period `k ≥ 3` — an infinite family, via the `q = 1` height. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_one_odd_forces","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_one_odd_forces","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L49-L61","doc":"**One-odd-step cycle forces the denominator equation.** The even chain plus\nthe single odd step force `((q+1)^k − (q²+q+1))·P_{k-1} = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.even_chain_collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.even_chain_collapse","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_one_odd_family.lean#L33-L47","doc":"**Even chain collapse.** A chain of even steps `Pᵢ₊₁·(q+1) = Pᵢ` for `i < k`\ntelescopes to `P₀ = (q+1)^k · P_k`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}